6-04-28T00:00:08.916Z","status":"pending"},"Ube593d6d8690c2e30fe2ea895d1f3e99":{"eventTitle":"高中教務會議","pushedAt":"2026-04-28T00:00:08.916Z","status":"pending"}}},"essay-context":{"U010bf9e8afc2bf7e0bddf9d6a904f1a8":{"expiresAt":1789031300098,"lastReply":"我先把你稿子的內容辨識出來（如有少數字詞我可能看錯，請確認）：\n\nEver since I was a child, I have cherished the hope that the world can be more peaceful. In recent years, more and more countries start to fight for the nature resources. Just like the war in Ilan, war not only cause dead but also lead damage to the enviornment. Because of the governents new policy, solider is forced to leave theyr family and loose their life. Moreover, the war may impacted nature enviornment or the habitant that animal live. Therefore, I hope that everyone can get together to make the world more peaceful.\n\nTo make this dream come ture, I will participate the International Organistation and do the thing that I can do to help the world more better. For example, I will take to the streets to protest against the goverment's wrong or raise awareness among those around us how we can make our enviornment and even the world more better. All in all, it is not easy to have a peaceful world but we still can do something small to protect the land we standing on.\n\n📌 整體評語\n你已經有兩段清楚的段落：第一段說明問題（戰爭的後果），第二段提出行動（個人可做的事）。優點是語意清楚，段落功能分明。最大的改進空間是：句法與拼字錯誤較多會影響分數；其次要把例證或個人經驗具體化、並把開頭/結尾寫得更有力以提升層次。\n\n1️⃣ 結構\n具體評語 + 建議\n- 目前你有「描述/問題段」＋「論述/行動段」，這符合基礎二段式結構，段落功能分明：第一段描述戰爭的負面影響，第二段寫你想做的事。\n- 建議：第一段可加入一個更具體的例證（例如你看過的新聞、一個親身目擊或一個數據），讓論述更有說服力。第二段可把行動分成 2–3 個具體步驟（例如：參加哪一類組織、具體如何宣傳、落實的時間或對象），並在最後加一個昇華句（社會/政策層次）。\n\n範例建議：\n- 在第一段補上具體例證：For example, when I visited Ilan last year, I saw…（示範句見下方「內容深度」）\n- 在第二段把行動列點：First, I will join X; Second, I will organize Y; Last, I will petition Z.\n\n2️⃣ 開頭與結尾\n具體評語 + 改寫範例\n- 你的開頭直接寫\"I have cherished the hope...\"，屬於直接陳述主題。學測佳作常用「漏斗式」開頭（情境/感官/第一人稱經驗）來吸引讀者。\n- 結尾現在有總結但較草率，建議加入首尾呼應或價值昇華，例如把「我所站的土地」和「下一代的未來」連結起來。\n\n漏斗式開頭範例（請選一種改寫風格套入原意）：\n1) 感官/場景型：\n- 改寫前：Ever since I was a child, I have cherished the hope that the world can be more peaceful.\n- 改寫後：When I heard the sirens and saw news footage of destroyed homes as a child, I quietly wished that one day the world would be peaceful again.\n(原因：以場景帶出情感，比直接陳述更有吸引力。)\n\n2) 個人經驗型：\n- 改寫前同上\n- 改寫後：As a child, I often fell asleep to the news of conflicts; those images made me long for a more peaceful world.\n(原因：第一人稱經驗拉近讀者距離。)\n\n結尾建議句型（昇華＋呼應）：\n- 改寫前：All in all, it is not easy to have a peaceful world but we still can do something small to protect the land we standing on.\n- 改寫後：All in all, achieving global peace is difficult, but if each of us takes small, steady actions—just as I will—then the land we stand on may become safer for future generations.\n(原因：呼應開頭的情感並提升到下一代/社會層次。)\n\n3️⃣ 論證與銜接詞\n具體評語 + 建議\n- 你使用了 Moreover、Therefore、For example、All in all，已知道使用連接詞。但部分地方的連接不夠組織化（例如沒有有序地列出理由）。\n- 建議：使用 First/Second/Finally 或 Firstly/Moreover/Lastly 來標示步驟或理由；避免只用同一種轉折詞或口語式連接。也可用結果型連接詞 (Consequently, As a result) 與讓步型 (Although / Even though)。\n\n可用替換詞（常用的替換）：\n- Moreover → Furthermore / In addition / What's more\n- Therefore → Consequently / As a result / Thus\n- For example → For instance / To illustrate / Take X as an example\n\n4️⃣ 詞彙與句型（列出 3–5 個可升級的詞彙/句型，附修改前後對照）\n列出重複或過於基礎的詞彙並提供替換：\n- more → increasingly / progressively / even more\n  - 改寫前：more and more countries start to fight for the nature resources.\n  - 改寫後：increasingly, countries have begun to compete for natural resources.\n- fight for → fight over / compete for /争夺 (英：fight over)\n  - 改寫前：fight for the nature resources\n  - 改寫後：fight over natural resources\n- damage → harm / cause damage to → cause environmental damage / devastate\n  - 改寫前：lead damage to the enviornment\n  - 改寫後：cause environmental damage\n- better → improve / make better / enhance\n  - 改寫前：help the world more better\n  - 改寫後：help improve the world / help make the world better\n\n句型進階示範（分詞構句、倒裝）\n- 改寫前：Because of the government's new policy, soldiers are forced to leave their families.\n- 改寫後（分詞構句）：Forced by the government's new policy, soldiers must leave their families.\n- 改寫前：It is not easy to have a peaceful world.\n- 改寫後（倒裝或強調）：Rarely has achieving world peace been easy.\n\n5️⃣ 文法與拼字（列出主要錯誤，附修正）\n我挑出會影響理解或評分的錯誤，採「原句 → 建議修正（簡短說明）」格式：\n\n- In recent years, more and more countries start to fight for the nature resources.\n  → In recent years, more and more countries have started to fight over natural resources.\n  (原因：時態需完成式；用 fight over + 名詞；natural resources 正確拼法與語序。)\n\n- Just like the war in Ilan, war not only cause dead but also lead damage to the enviornment.\n  → Just like the war in Ilan, war not only causes deaths but also causes environmental damage.\n  (原因：主詞 war 為單數，動詞需加 s；\"dead\" → \"deaths\"；\"lead damage to\" 不自然，改成 \"causes environmental damage\"。)\n\n- Because of the governents new policy, solider is forced to leave theyr family and loose their life.\n  → Because of the government's new policies, soldiers are forced to leave their families and sometimes lose their lives.\n  (原因：governments → government's (所有格)；solider → soldiers（複數）; theyr → their；lose 拼法；life → lives 若泛指多數則用複數。)\n\n- Moreover, the war may impacted nature enviornment or the habitant that animal live.\n  → Moreover, the war may impact the natural environment or the habitats where animals live.\n  (原因：impacted → impact (不定詞/原形) 或 may have impacted；enviornment → environment；habitant → habitat；語序 & where 子句更通順。)\n\n- To make this dream come ture, I will participate the International Organistation and do the thing that I can do to help the world more better.\n  → To make this dream come true, I will participate in international organizations and do what I can to help make the world better.\n  (原因：ture → true；participate in；Organistation → organisation/organization；do the thing that I can do → do what I can；more better → better。)\n\n- I will take to the streets to protest against the goverment's wrong or raise awareness among those around us how we can make our enviornment and even the world more better.\n  → I will take to the streets to protest against the government's wrongdoings and raise awareness among people about how we can improve our environment and the world.\n  (原因：goverment → government；語意更清晰的表達；修正 \"more better\"。)\n\n- All in all, it is not easy to have a peaceful world but we still can do something small to protect the land we standing on.\n  → All in all, it is not easy to achieve a peaceful world, but we can still do small things to protect the land we stand on.\n  (原因：achieve 比 have 精確；we standing on → we stand on。)\n\n✅ 下一步建議（1–2 個優先修改項目）\n1. 先把所有明顯的拼字與文法錯誤修正（我上面列出的錯誤優先改），確保句子能被評閱者快速理解。  \n2. 補一個具體而個人的例子（約一到兩句），並把第二段的行動具體化（分成 2–3 個步驟或措施），最後把結尾改為首尾呼應並升華到社會/下一代層次。\n\n額外示範（把你原文做一小段精修示例，保留你的意思）：\n原句：Just like the war in Ilan, war not only cause dead but also lead damage to the enviornment.\n建議改：Just like the war in Ilan, war not only causes deaths but also causes severe environmental damage.\n\n原句：To make this dream come ture, I will participate the International Organistation and do the thing that I can do to help the world more better.\n建議改：To make this dream come true, I will join international organizations, participate in peaceful campaigns, and do what I can to improve our world.\n\n最後鼓勵一句：你已經抓到題目的主軸（世界和平與行動），只要把語言（文法、拼字）處理乾淨、把例證具體化、再強化開頭與結尾的情感與層次，就能明顯提升分數。需要的話我可以幫你把全文逐句改寫成更正式的學測版本，或只幫你修改第二段的行動部分—你想先從哪裡開始？","updatedAt":1789030700098},"U1e6470f5d2a51d089f046358e664ff41":{"expiresAt":1789718341854,"lastReply":"📌 整體評語\n你已經抓到題目的核心（物價上漲與升學壓力），文章有個人觀點與結論，語氣親切自然，結尾有情感昇華（感恩祖國），這些都是很加分的元素。最大改進空間在於：句子文法（主動/被動、單複數、冠詞、動詞形態）與銜接詞使用需更精準，並補一個更具體的個人例證來提升說服力。\n\n1️⃣ 結構\n評語：整篇大致可分為（1）說明問題與個人感受、（2）比較與理由、（3）結論（感恩）。結構已有二段式主體＋結尾呼應，段落功能基本具備，但每段的主題句可以更明確。\n建議：\n- 第一段（描述現況＋個人感受）：在開頭一句明確寫出主題句，例如 “Recently inflation and school pressure have affected my life.” 再展開細節。\n- 第二段（比較與論述）：把比較放在段首句，接著用一個具體例子或數據支持（見下方「內容深度」）。\n- 結尾：把個人經驗與對社會/政策層面的反思銜接（例如呼籲政府或提出學生可行的紓壓方法）。\n\n2️⃣ 開頭與結尾\n評語：你以「Thanks for your warm care!」直接回覆，很自然但屬於直述式開頭；學測優秀卷常用「漏斗式」：由具體場景/感官或個人經驗切入，再引出主題。\n建議改寫範例（英文）：\n- 漏斗式開頭範例 1：\n  原句：Thanks for your warm care!\n  改寫：When I wake up to the sound of morning news about rising prices, I sometimes feel anxious. Thanks for your warm care — I want to tell you how I cope with inflation and school pressure.\n- 漏斗式開頭範例 2（感官描寫）： \n  原句：Thanks for your warm care!\n  改寫：The smell of instant noodles and the news of another price hike are common in my daily life. Thank you for your concern—here is how I feel about life in Taiwan now.\n\n結尾建議：\n- 現有結尾有情感，但可更強化首尾呼應：例如在開頭提到的具體場景再現，並升華成對社會的期望或行動呼籲。\n  範例：Although prices keep rising, I remain grateful and hope the government and schools can offer more support to young people.\n\n3️⃣ 論證與銜接詞\n評語：你使用了 However、Although、Besides、Anyway 等，但有時位置或搭配不太自然（例如 \"However, despite these difficulties\" 有重複轉折感）。\n建議：\n- 以清晰邏輯標示段落：First, Second/Moreover, In contrast, Finally。\n- 避免重複（若已用 However，再用 Besides 可改為 Furthermore / On the other hand / In contrast）。\n- 範例替換表：\n  - However → Nevertheless / Yet\n  - Besides → Furthermore / Moreover\n  - On the other hand → Conversely\n\n4️⃣ 詞彙與句型（列出 3–5 個可升級的詞彙/句型，附修改前後對照）\n- drain me everyday → 原句：the pressure of schoolwork really drain me everyday\n  建議：the pressure of schoolwork really drains me every day\n  進階詞彙：exhausts me / wears me out\n- agreeable life → 原句：I still live a agreeable life\n  建議：I still lead a comfortable/satisfying life\n  進階詞彙：a reasonably comfortable life / a decent quality of life\n- economical → 原句：the prices of Taiwan are still economical\n  建議：prices in Taiwan are still relatively affordable\n  進階詞彙：comparatively low / more affordable than in many countries\n- Studies stress → 原句：Studies stress, on the other hand, is also not a big deal to me\n  建議：Study-related stress, on the other hand, is not a big deal for me\n  句型升級（分詞構句示範）：\n  原句：I can chat with my peers and discuss the problems I encountered...\n  改寫（分詞構句）：By chatting with my peers and discussing problems in homework, I can reduce my stress a lot.\n\n5️⃣ 文法與拼字（列出主要錯誤，附修正）\n- 原句 → 建議修正（簡短原因）\n1. \"the pressure of schoolwork really drain me everyday\" → \"the pressure of schoolwork really drains me every day\"\n  （主詞與動詞一致；every day 兩字分開）\n2. \"I still live a agreeable life.\" → \"I still live an agreeable life.\" → 更建議 \"I still lead a comfortable life.\" \n  （冠詞使用 a/an；語義上 lead 更自然）\n3. \"the government would adjust / invest wage\" → \"the government would adjust wages / raise the minimum wage\"\n  （wage 應為複數或用 \"raise wages\"；invest wage 不合語法）\n4. \"Studies stress, on the other hand, is also not a big deal to me\" → \"Study stress, on the other hand, is not a big deal to me\"\n  （名詞順序與主詞動詞一致）\n5. \"which helps me reduce my pressure a lot.\" → \"which helps me reduce my stress a lot.\" 或 \"which helps me relieve my stress.\"\n  （native collocation: reduce stress / relieve stress）\n6. \"the prices of Taiwan are still economical\" → \"prices in Taiwan are still relatively affordable\"\n  （economical 用法不自然）\n\n✅ 下一步建議（最應優先修改的兩件事）\n1. 修改第一段的文法錯誤（主動詞時態、單複數、冠詞）：把開頭三句完全修通順，然後讀給自己聽，確保語氣自然。重點句我幫你改一遍（英文範例）：\n   原句：The inflation in Taiwan has escalated significantly, and the pressure of schoolwork really drain me everyday.\n   建議：Inflation in Taiwan has escalated significantly, and the pressure of schoolwork really drains me every day.\n2. 加入一個具體個人例證（1–2 句）：寫一個你和同學討論作業或某次物價影響生活的真實小故事，讓論點更有說服力。\n   範例句（英文）：\"Last month I and two classmates pooled money to buy groceries after noticing prices had gone up; by sharing errands we saved time and felt less anxious.\"\n\n最後提醒\n- 開頭可以從小場景切入（提高分數機會），段落首句務必明確。文章已有溫度與反思，只要修正文法、加一個具體例證並稍微強化轉折與結論，就能再往佳作靠攏。做完修改後可以再傳給我，我會幫你看第二版的細節。加油，你已經有很好的材料！","updatedAt":1789717741854},"U56213af13357fee33663b04b9352519a":{"expiresAt":1789099070785,"lastReply":"📸 圖片說明\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n照片是一張手寫的英文作文，內容第一段是在總結一個公園的訪客調查（關於遊樂設施、服務、環境和食物），第二段描述作者對遊樂場的回憶與理由。底部有老師用紅筆的回饋。\n\n✏️ 初階改寫版本\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\nThe chart shows visitors' comments about a park. According to the survey, visitors have different opinions about rides, service, the environment and food. Visitor A likes the friendly employees and thinks the rides are good. Visitor B says the staff are friendly but the food choices are not many. Visitor C thinks most things are good, but the toilets need more space. All visitors hope the park will be better in the future.\n\nI remember the playground at the park. This part was the most impressive for me. First, I can play with my friends there and have fun. We do many activities and learn to work together. Second, the games help us build confidence and try new things. In the end, the playground helps us improve and make better friends.\n\n📝 關鍵用詞說明\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n1️⃣ survey - 調查（收集別人意見或資料的過程）  \n2️⃣ visitor - 訪客、參觀者（來到某地的人）  \n3️⃣ playground - 遊樂場、操場（孩子們玩耍的地方）\n\n💪 寫得很好！繼續加油！","updatedAt":1789098470785}},"example-cache":{"000069fb5a9a7d70a62c05cc38584a1a":{"createdAt":1785074064299,"data":{"sentence":"She quickly grabbed her phone before it fell off the table.","translation":"她迅速地抓住她的手機，以免它從桌子上掉下來。"}},"000daa2279cd09d3e018404b95dec975":{"createdAt":1787050102718,"data":{"sentence":"I need to install new software on my computer before I can start working.","translation":"在我開始工作之前，我需要在電腦上安裝新的軟體。"}},"0016227da7d8b7e7ff271a5e8c687df9":{"createdAt":1782574862162,"data":{"sentence":"The teacher had to intervene when the argument between the two students became too heated.","translation":"當兩名學生之間的爭執變得過於激烈時，老師不得不進行調停。"}},"002eb97af54476460ce0202301bd20d2":{"createdAt":1782171382675,"data":{"sentence":"I decided to enroll in a Spanish language course next semester.","translation":"我決定在下個學期報名參加西班牙語課程。"}},"0037a624e57a2af6cce8a4be95400ff2":{"createdAt":1781881142760,"data":{"sentence":"The new marketing campaign had a significant effect on the company's sales figures.","translation":"這次新的行銷活動對公司的銷售數字產生了顯著的影響。"}},"00540e30d95e52f1fedcb667766a8cbc":{"createdAt":1785765434724,"data":{"sentence":"She applied a light powder to her face to mattify her skin before the photoshoot.","translation":"她在拍照前在臉上撲了一層輕薄的粉來消除皮膚的光澤。"}},"00765d0686d07479714beb2f6e72fe7e":{"createdAt":1788589934225,"data":{"sentence":"This new software update will enable users to access the application from their mobile devices.","translation":"這個新的軟體更新將使用戶能夠從他們的行動裝置存取該應用程式。"}},"007745b91d4a45620a5dea0b8efb2666":{"createdAt":1784278202707,"data":{"sentence":"She typically arrives at the office by 8 AM every morning.","translation":"她通常每天早上八點前到達辦公室。"}},"007d68ad2752614d31b1137bad91450a":{"createdAt":1788953124384,"data":{"sentence":"The so-called experts failed to predict the market crash.","translation":"這些所謂的專家未能預測到市場崩盤。"}},"00812b95ec6c1b5225f4bb170a7e62b8":{"createdAt":1785744109846,"data":{"sentence":"The young athlete has great potential to become a professional player if he continues training hard.","translation":"這位年輕運動員如果持續努力訓練，就有很大的潛力成為職業選手。"}},"0081f612721d75a2522ab7f47def1742":{"createdAt":1781767707140,"data":{"sentence":"I can't stand the loud noise from the construction site next door.","translation":"我無法忍受隔壁建築工地發出的巨大噪音。"}},"008b03e60cca47009748bf828d36a398":{"createdAt":1785852315042,"data":{"sentence":"The public expressed outrage over the government's decision to cut funding for schools and hospitals.","translation":"公眾對政府削減學校和醫院經費的決定表示憤慨。"}},"00a4f677f1f84b3993644ce1289d75d3":{"createdAt":1781451235736,"data":{"sentence":"The new software tools facilitate better communication between team members across different departments.","translation":"新的軟體工具促進了不同部門的團隊成員之間的更好溝通。"}},"00a67888356fee8e99a34124f5143c65":{"createdAt":1786951649382,"data":{"sentence":"The word 'don't' is a contraction of 'do not'.","translation":"單詞'don't'是'do not'的縮寫形式。"}},"00ab8e51a4713634db108cdbec7c3395":{"createdAt":1787982076846,"data":{"sentence":"The company decided to lay off 200 employees due to the economic downturn.","translation":"由於經濟衰退，該公司決定解雇200名員工。"}},"00b671d16650c6731dcc10162ea33ac9":{"createdAt":1785479990119,"data":{"sentence":"I need to brush up on my Spanish before my trip to Madrid next month.","translation":"在下個月去馬德里旅行前，我需要溫習一下我的西班牙語。"}},"00bacc0bb63ebd1e27030286bad1afcc":{"createdAt":1787306051488,"data":{"sentence":"Before you make a decision, hold your horses and think it through carefully.","translation":"在你做決定之前，稍安勿躁，仔細想清楚。"}},"00ef61d591a7e637977db9469f788996":{"createdAt":1784503163666,"data":{"sentence":"The old man accumulated considerable wealth through decades of hard work and smart investments.","translation":"這位老人通過數十年的辛苦工作和聰明的投資積累了相當可觀的財富。"}},"011f30b60c3c59feec582b57f178a4c7":{"createdAt":1782056458804,"data":{"sentence":"After waiting in line for hours, Sarah felt a deep sense of disappointment when the concert was cancelled.","translation":"在排隊等待數小時後，莎拉在演唱會被取消時感到深深的失望。"}},"0120ca36e9bc996875a09d51f869d31a":{"createdAt":1784250609976,"data":{"sentence":"The volcano erupted suddenly, sending ash and lava into the sky.","translation":"火山突然爆發，將灰燼和熔岩噴向天空。"}},"0127edb2152ea0ba9bf2ddb0730cdfba":{"createdAt":1781281000178,"data":{"sentence":"In this region, the economy is dominated by agriculture, with farming dominantly shaping the local culture and lifestyle.","translation":"在這個地區，經濟以農業為主，農業支配性地塑造了當地的文化和生活方式。"}},"012d591238adc15b7412daefb9cff525":{"createdAt":1782085429764,"data":{"sentence":"The explorer set forth on a journey across the uncharted wilderness.","translation":"那位探險家出發前往未知的荒野進行一次旅程。"}},"012f4bee05d6545a4ef66dd0017ce554":{"createdAt":1782984517473,"data":{"sentence":"The opening scene of the movie was absolutely breathtaking with its sweeping views of the mountain landscape.","translation":"這部電影的開場場景絕對令人驚嘆，展現了壯闊的山景風景。"}},"013bdfed28467b474eb610c09ee5e133":{"createdAt":1786362284482,"data":{"sentence":"She no longer works at that company after she decided to pursue her dream of becoming a teacher.","translation":"在她決定追求成為教師的夢想後，她不再在那家公司工作。"}},"014c8d821937fe96012fceac70852629":{"createdAt":1787833114051,"data":{"sentence":"The new software is functioning smoothly after the recent update.","translation":"新軟體在最近的更新後運作得很順利。"}},"014d588366378d9fa44375f3a0b1c2bd":{"createdAt":1788516946914,"data":{"sentence":"His apology was in no sense sincere, as he showed no remorse whatsoever.","translation":"他的道歉決不真誠，因為他絲毫沒有表現出悔意。"}},"015111eaa99520f5115b12f11fc25b48":{"createdAt":1784444637589,"data":{"sentence":"The angry customer threatened to call the police if the store didn't refund his money.","translation":"那位憤怒的顧客威脅說，如果店家不退款，他就會報警。"}},"0152d0a33a91b320f079cbff514f9853":{"createdAt":1787485243106,"data":{"sentence":"The myth of Pandora's Box has been passed down through Western culture for thousands of years.","translation":"潘多拉魔盒的神話已經在西方文化中流傳了數千年。"}},"015e9dacde12e369bc59272689a4286c":{"createdAt":1782351234846,"data":{"sentence":"The farmer's market has a vegetable stall where locals buy fresh produce every weekend.","translation":"農夫市場裡有一個蔬菜攤位，當地人每個週末都在那裡購買新鮮農產品。"}},"0165941a66a4a980e72554f672ab410a":{"createdAt":1785491615226,"data":{"sentence":"She gave an emotional speech at her father's funeral, tears streaming down her face as she shared her memories.","translation":"她在父親的葬禮上做了一場感情充沛的演講，淚流滿面地分享了她的回憶。"}},"0176d1d1597cc7f9572003aec6ad072e":{"createdAt":1782225339673,"data":{"sentence":"The famous director made a cameo appearance in the final scene of her latest film.","translation":"這位著名導演在她最新電影的最後一幕中客串演出。"}},"017f98c14bbe9b4230779c98f0250218":{"createdAt":1788060346017,"data":{"sentence":"The undercover detective decided to pose as a wealthy businessman to infiltrate the criminal organization.","translation":"那位臥底偵探決定假扮成一名富有的商人，以滲透進入犯罪組織。"}},"0189faf5d1960528170b39bd51f775c8":{"createdAt":1786778153896,"data":{"sentence":"The company implemented new processes to improve efficiency in their manufacturing department.","translation":"該公司實施了新的流程以提高其製造部門的效率。"}},"01bfc4cd074e390d3a1944ac55f65fbf":{"createdAt":1782705281211,"data":{"sentence":"The 19th-century British political movement of antidisestablishmentarianism fiercely opposed the separation of the Church of England from state power.","translation":"十九世紀英國反對教會與國家分離主義的政治運動激烈反對英國國教與國家權力的分離。"}},"01c599e434a67ba9bb000166b7c53cf2":{"createdAt":1786158807728,"data":{"sentence":"The company is currently in a transition period as it shifts from traditional manufacturing to digital production.","translation":"該公司目前正處於過渡期，正在從傳統製造業轉變為數位生產。"}},"01c9cc7b1774462c5d623398fd955b58":{"createdAt":1781487410545,"data":{"sentence":"The farmer sprayed pesticide on his crops to eliminate the pest that was destroying his vegetables.","translation":"農民在他的莊稼上噴灑殺蟲劑，以消滅正在摧毀他蔬菜的害蟲。"}},"01d51c4b966b8dc514ebe938f01edcf9":{"createdAt":1781881293067,"data":{"sentence":"The prisoner managed to escape from the jail by digging a tunnel under the fence.","translation":"那名囚犯通過在柵欄下挖掘隧道設法逃出了監獄。"}},"01e7fe4db7d53798d3dbed315fa8f5a8":{"createdAt":1783572456765,"data":{"sentence":"Graduating from university was a major achievement that required years of hard work and dedication.","translation":"從大學畢業是一項重大成就，需要多年的努力和奉獻。"}},"01edef49ca368eac954afd1f9def2968":{"createdAt":1781530550377,"data":{"sentence":"The company hired an external firm to conduct an annual audit of their financial records.","translation":"該公司聘請一家外部公司對其財務紀錄進行年度審計。"}},"01f8e780f2201360ff3be9e8cd9ce00f":{"createdAt":1786419066567,"data":{"sentence":"The board of directors approved the new budget proposal at yesterday's meeting.","translation":"董事會在昨天的會議上批准了新的預算提案。"}},"020b20868f2581801e1851dbd546c2bd":{"createdAt":1789600121729,"data":{"sentence":"He came from a respectable family and maintained a good reputation throughout his career.","translation":"他出身於一個可敬的家庭，並在整個職業生涯中保持著良好的聲譽。"}},"021f177866382f63b167c08aa76d32c0":{"createdAt":1781665502224,"data":{"sentence":"We visited the old cemetery on a quiet Sunday afternoon to pay respects to our ancestors.","translation":"我們在一個寧靜的星期天下午拜訪了老墓地，向我們的祖先致敬。"}},"0229880ae62fc993db9bf53181f3fe0c":{"createdAt":1783556462693,"data":{"sentence":"The young child nearly drowned in the